{"step_index":98,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-15T08:58:00Z","model":"gemini-3.8-flash-high","input_tokens":4021,"cache_read_tokens":97797,"output_tokens":1768,"thinking":"The server is not gzipping the CSS bundle, despite the presence of compression middleware. The reported `Content-Length` confirms this. Investigating the server code, the compression middleware uses a `zlib` library. The middleware is intended to compress static text assets.\n\n\nThe compression middleware has a conditional check: it only compresses responses with a 200 status code. Further examination of the code reveals that responses are not compressed if they already have `Content-Encoding` set. Initial hypothesis: the CSS bundle's `Content-Encoding` might be inadvertently set elsewhere. Another section of code appears to handle the response body and skips compression if the response has already been encoded.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"node -e '\nconst express = require(\"express\");\nconst zlib = require(\"zlib\");\nconst path = require(\"path\");\nconst http = require(\"http\");\n\nconst app = express();\napp.use((req, res, next) => {\n    console.log(\"Middleware called for path:\", req.path);\n    const ae = req.headers[\"accept-encoding\"] || \"\";\n    if (req.method !== \"GET\" || !/\\bgzip\\b/.test(ae)) return next();\n    if (!/\\.(html?|css|js|mjs|json|svg|xml|txt|map|webmanifest)$/i.test(req.path)) return next();\n\n    const rawWrite = res.write.bind(res);\n    const rawEnd   = res.end.bind(res);\n    const chunks   = [];\n    let finished   = false;\n\n    res.write = function (chunk, enc, cb) {\n        if (chunk) chunks.push(Buffer.isBuffer(chunk) ? chunk : Buffer.from(chunk, enc));\n        if (typeof cb === \"function\") cb();\n        return true;\n    };\n    res.end = function (chunk, enc, cb) {\n        if (finished) return;\n        finished = true;\n        if (typeof chunk === \"function\") { cb = chunk; chunk = null; enc = null; }\n        else if (typeof enc === \"function\") { cb = enc; enc = null; }\n        if (chunk) chunks.push(Buffer.isBuffer(chunk) ? chunk : Buffer.from(chunk, enc));\n        const body = Buffer.concat(chunks);\n        console.log(\"res.end called! body length:\", body.length, \"headersSent:\", res.headersSent);\n\n        if (res.statusCode !== 200 || body.length === 0 || res.getHeader(\"Content-Encoding\")) {\n            console.log(\"Skipping gzip:\", { statusCode: res.statusCode, len: body.length, ce: res.getHeader(\"Content-Encoding\") });\n            if (body.length) { res.setHeader(\"Content-Length\", body.length); rawWrite(body); }\n            return rawEnd(cb);\n        }\n        zlib.gzip(body, (err, zipped) => {\n            console.log(\"gzip finished, zipped len:\", zipped ? zipped.length : err);\n            if (err) { res.setHeader(\"Content-Length\", body.length); rawWrite(body); return rawEnd(cb); }\n            try {\n                res.setHeader(\"Content-Encoding\", \"gzip\");\n                res.setHeader(\"Vary\", \"Accept-Encoding\");\n                res.setHeader(\"Content-Length\", zipped.length);\n                rawWrite(zipped);\n                rawEnd(cb);\n            } catch(e) {\n                console.error(\"Error setting headers:\", e.message);\n                rawWrite(body);\n                rawEnd(cb);\n            }\n        });\n    };\n    next();\n});\n\napp.use(express.static(path.join(__dirname, \"frontend\")));\n\nconst server = app.listen(3099, () => {\n    http.get(\"http://localhost:3099/css/bundle-home.min.css\", { headers: { \"Accept-Encoding\": \"gzip\" } }, (res) => {\n        console.log(\"Response headers:\", res.headers);\n        server.close();\n    });\n});\n'","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolSummary":"Debug gzip middleware"}}]}
